##" Every run of one eval set: how each package version scored and ran.
##| artifact { layout=linear title="Eval history"
  tiles=[
    intro { kind=text },
    "versions -> by_version",
    tags { kind=text },
    "tag_scores -> by_tag",
    recent_runs { kind=text },
    "runs -> recent",
    "tag_scores -> tag_by_run"
  ]
}
|##
import "history.malloy"

##|(markdown) intro
## 1. By package version

Each version's newest full answer run and newest query replay. `fixed` and
`broke` count cases that flipped against the version before, over the cases
both runs could be compared on. A version with no full run shows its replay
only. Rebuilt from the runs by `eval.py history`, so it is never edited.
|##

##|(markdown) tags
## 2. By tag

Pass rate per tag across the answer runs here. The lowest tags are where a
slice is worth working on: fix the slice, then confirm on the whole set.
|##

##|(markdown) recent_runs
## 3. Recent runs

Every run, newest first, with the experiment it belongs to. "main" is the
package itself; an experiment is served beside it (`eval.py experiment`).
|##
